# Architecture Plan: alex-1883-cardbox

## Project shape
- Vite + React + TypeScript single-page Cardbox inbox app.
- Tailwind CSS is configured in `tailwind.config.js` and all app-wide visual tokens are exposed as CSS custom properties in `src/styles/global.css`.
- Static frontend only: no backend, database, CORS, or runtime proxy-specific code is needed for Issue #25.

## Module structure and file organization
- `src/main.tsx`: React entrypoint, imports global styles.
- `src/App.tsx`: Top-level application composition.
- `src/components/`: Reusable UI primitives such as message cards, indicators, sender highlight, and compose controls.
- `src/views/`: Screen-level inbox and reader views.
- `src/store/`: Client-side state and local-storage persistence helpers/tests.
- `src/types/`: Shared message and store-related TypeScript models.
- `src/fixtures/`: Seed inbox content.
- `src/styles/global.css`: Source of runtime CSS custom properties and Tailwind component classes. `--color-neutral-base` drives the page/app background through `bg-neutral-base`.
- `src/styles/tokens.ts`: TypeScript mirror of design-token color channels for tests and shared token metadata.
- `src/styles/tokens.test.ts`: Guards token mapping, contrast, and theme-token integrity.

## Issue dependency plan
- Issue #25, "Change neutral base background to light blue", is independent of feature/store work.
- It depends only on the existing token layer from `src/styles/global.css`, `src/styles/tokens.ts`, and `tailwind.config.js`.
- No new dependencies are required.

## Key design decisions for Issue #25
- Treat the neutral base color as a design token, not a component-local style.
- Update both the CSS custom property (`--color-neutral-base`) and the TypeScript token mirror (`themeColorChannels.neutralBase`) to the same light-blue RGB channels so runtime styling and tests stay aligned.
- Update `index.html` `theme-color` to the matching hex color so browser chrome aligns with the new background.
- Preserve existing neutral surface, border, ink, muted, and accent tokens unless tests or contrast checks indicate a necessary adjustment.
- Validate with the existing Node toolchain: `npm test`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build`.
